-- check/bad (project): `Wraps` holds a `Handle` whose only `compare` is
-- private to `Handles` (A.54, A.50).
--
-- The gate asked whether the declaring module has a value called `compare`,
-- `pub` or not, so this module derived an ordering for `Wraps` — and the
-- part for its `Handle` was `err`, because the module rule cannot reach a
-- private value from here. A clean compile and a table naming nothing.
import Handles exposing (Handle)


pub type Wraps
    = Wraps Handle


pub before : Wraps, Wraps -> Bool
before a b = a < b
